From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:02:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Join the branches: HD textures follow gfx.hd_textures,
 threaded settings menu, frame cap in the flip limiter

- HD textures read gfx.hd_textures from the port settings (Auto = best pack present), flush and reload live when the
  setting changes, enable the greyed row when a pack is found; the old HD_TEXTURES env maps to a developer override.
- HD replacement filtering: the replacement keeps its own mips (no glGenerateMipmap over it); gfx.mipmaps=off uses level 0
  only, gfx.texture_filter=original keeps minification linear and follows the game's filter for magnification.
- The settings menu with the GE thread: the guest runs the modal loop under the kernel pause and posts every paint,
  screenshot and event pump to the GE thread (the GL context is the GE thread's); the menu is never painted while it is
  updated.
- perf.frame_cap is the guest-side flip limiter (sceDisplaySetFrameBuf): 60 = one flip per refresh, 30 = every other, off
  = none. GameProfile::frame_vblanks only places the interpolation grid and never limited anything.
- perf.threaded_renderer comes from the port settings; the desktop executable runs the guest on a thread of its own and the
  GE thread on the main one (INFECTED_THREADED_RENDERER=0 for the old single thread).
- The settings chord does not fire with L or R held (START+SELECT+L+R is the Vita application's exit).
- ge_replay: --hd follow, --port-switch FLIP:KEY=VALUE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

